Do not start, stop, borrow, or change eye drops based on a social-media post or another child's prescription. Ask what the proposed approach is intended to do, what is known and uncertain, how often the child will be reviewed, and what to do if discomfort or another concern develops. More than one approach may be considered in some circumstances, but a specialist must decide whether that is appropriate. The aim is a clear, safe plan—not a promise of zero progression or freedom from glasses.
