The eye focuses light through the cornea and lens onto the retina. If the eye’s focusing shape or length causes light not to focus clearly, the result is a refractive error such as myopia, hyperopia or astigmatism. Spectacles and contact lenses correct that focus while they are being worn. Refractive surgery changes the optical properties of the eye to reduce dependence on those aids. LASIK is one type of refractive surgery; it is not a treatment for every cause of blurred vision.

