Uveitis may cause pain, redness, light sensitivity, floaters or blurred vision, but symptoms depend on which part is inflamed and can sometimes be subtle. Diabetic retinal disease may cause no early warning at all. Record when a change began, whether it affects one or both eyes, and how quickly it is progressing. Sudden visual loss, severe pain, a curtain, or flashes with new floaters calls for urgent professional help. A home vision grid can help someone notice change but cannot diagnose or rule out disease.
