Chemical splashes and penetrating injuries are emergencies. For a chemical exposure, begin rinsing the eye immediately with clean, lukewarm running water and seek emergency care; do not delay rinsing while searching for special drops. Do not rub an injured eye or try to remove an embedded object. A painful red eye with declining vision, sudden clouding or discharge should also be assessed urgently. Symptoms are clues, not a way to distinguish infection from allergy or another eye condition at home.
