Tell the clinician about contact-lens wear and cleaning habits, eye rubbing, allergies, recent trauma, previous infections, eye drops and family history of corneal disease. Eye rubbing may be associated with corneal problems and can aggravate irritation; ask for help managing itch rather than rubbing. Do not self-diagnose keratoconus from a glasses prescription or a family member’s experience. A specialist can say whether a corneal-shape examination or further assessment is indicated.
