In adults, a new turn, sudden double vision, drooping eyelid, severe headache, weakness, speech difficulty, eye pain or vision loss needs urgent medical assessment, especially when symptoms start abruptly. Do not cover or patch an adult’s eye as a substitute for medical care without professional direction. Take a photograph if it helps show an intermittent turn, but it cannot replace an examination. The clinician needs to know when symptoms began and whether they are constant, episodic or changing.
