The cause of a squint is not always obvious from the outside. Family history, eye development, refractive error, health conditions, injury and other factors may be relevant. An adult’s new misalignment can have a different set of causes from a child’s longstanding one. Share any past eye examinations, glasses, patching or operations and relevant general medical history. Avoid blaming a child or assuming the condition will resolve without assessment; early evaluation helps determine what, if anything, needs treatment.
