Bring current spectacles and previous prescriptions, photographs that show an intermittent turn, and reports of earlier patching or surgery. Tell the clinician whether double vision is present, when it started, what direction the image shifts, and if covering either eye changes it. Some new adult-onset cases need investigation beyond the eye alignment itself; the clinician will decide based on findings. Ask whether amblyopia is present, how each eye sees, and which results will guide the next step.
