Childhood cataracts, eyelid problems, corneal conditions and inherited retinal or optic-nerve conditions are less common but can matter greatly for development. Prematurity and family history can raise the need for closer attention, but they do not automatically mean that a child has an eye disease. Share relevant birth and health history with the clinician. Avoid internet diagnosis and avoid blaming a child for not reporting vision problems. An examination should explain which condition is present and how the family can support treatment.
