Request a written estimate that distinguishes the surgical fee from pre-operative tests, medicines, follow-up, enhancement policy and complication management. Confirm the name of the surgeon responsible for care and who will see you at each follow-up. These practical details are part of informed consent because cost and continuity can affect whether a patient can complete the plan. Do not let a package description replace an explanation of the medical procedure and its risks.

