Before the family leaves, make sure the next review date is clear and that someone knows how to arrange it. Ask what symptoms should bring the child back sooner, how to reach the clinic with a question, and whether school should receive any written recommendation. If the prescription changes, ask for an updated copy and clarify whether old glasses remain useful as a backup. Keeping the child involved in these steps helps build age-appropriate responsibility while adults continue to supervise treatment.
