Before leaving, write down the agreed next step, any additional test, the name of the team to contact and the symptoms that need urgent attention. If you decide to monitor rather than operate, ask when the next examination is due and how to return earlier if sight changes. If surgery is chosen, wait for the treating team’s instructions before changing medicines or booking travel. A clear plan makes it easier to make a decision without feeling rushed and helps the caregiver provide the right practical support.
