Keep copies of the pre-operative test results, consent information, receipt or estimate, prescriptions and follow-up instructions. These records support continuity if you move, need another opinion or seek care for a later problem. Make sure family members understand that your personal information and decision are yours; do not feel obliged to proceed because someone has paid a deposit or travelled with you. Elective eye surgery should be based on an informed choice that remains comfortable after the consultation ends.
